"Filing and Forms | United States Court of Appeals for the Ninth Circuit (https://www.ca9.uscourts.gov/forms/)\nciteturn1414view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn1409view1\",\"lineno\":70}); Redirected to URL: https://www.ca9.uscourts.gov/filing/; Total lines: 108\nL0: cite0†United States Court of Appeals for the Ninth Circuit L1: \nL2: Chief Judge Mary H. Murguia\nL3: \nL4: [Button: Menu]\nL5: \nL6: cite1†Image: Close L7: \nL8:   * cite2†Decisions L9:   * cite3†Cases and Hearings L10:   * cite4†Filing and Forms L11:   * cite5†For Attorneys L12:   * cite6†Rules L13:   * cite7†Guides and Resources L14:   * cite8†Mediation L15:   * cite9†About L16: \nL17:   * cite10†Courts of the Ninth Circuit†www.ce9.uscourts.gov L18:   * cite11†Bankruptcy Appellate Panel†www.bap9.uscourts.gov L19: \nL20: Search [Input] cite12†Image: Search L21: # Filing and Forms\nL22: \nL23: “Filing” is the process of giving the Clerk of the Court an official document to enter into a case’s files or records. Often, you’ll use a form to do so.\nL24: \nL25: ## Filing Options\nL26: \nL27: ### If you're an attorney or court reporter\nL28: \nL29: You must file documents electronically using cite13†ACMS .\nL30: \nL31: cite14†LEARN ABOUT E-FILING L32: ### If you're representing yourself\nL33: \nL34: You can file documents:\nL35: \nL36:   * Electronically through cite13†ACMS L37: \nL38:   * Electronically through the court's cite15†online submission system L39: \nL40:   * By U.S. mail\nL41: \nL42:   * By dropping them off at the Browning Courthouse in San Francisco\nL43: \nL44: cite16†LEARN MORE L45: \nL46: ## Motions\nL47: \nL48: If you want to ask the court to do something in your case, you need to file a motion. A motion is a written request of the court.\nL49: \nL50: cite17†LEARN ABOUT MOTIONS L51: ## Briefs\nL52: \nL53: A brief is a written document that explains a party’s legal and factual arguments.\nL54: \nL55: cite18†LEARN ABOUT BRIEFS L56: \nL57: ## Excerpts of Record\nL58: \nL59: Excerpts of record are a set of lower court documents that the parties compile and file with the appeals court.\nL60: \nL61: cite19†LEARN ABOUT EXCERPTS OF RECORD L62: \nL63: ## Sealed Documents\nL64: \nL65: If you want to file a document under seal, you must file a motion to seal or a notice of sealing.\nL66: \nL67: cite20†LEARN ABOUT SEALED DOCUMENTS L68: ## Disclosure Statements\nL69: \nL70: A disclosure statement gives the court information to determine whether a judge might be disqualified from participating in a case.\nL71: \nL72: cite21†LEARN ABOUT DISCLOSURE STATEMENTS L73: \nL74: ## Forms\nL75: \nL76: The court provides forms in fillable PDF format with instructions.\nL77: \nL78: cite22†BROWSE ALL FORMS L79: \nL80: ## Fees\nL81: \nL82: Fees for filing and bar admission.\nL83: \nL84: cite23†SEE ALL FEES L85: ## More Help\nL86: \nL87: For more help with the appeal process, review the Appeal Process page.\nL88: \nL89: cite24†LEARN MORE L90: \nL91: Last updated September 29, 2026\nL92: \nL93: cite25†Return to Top L94: \nL95: United States Court of Appeals for the Ninth Circuit\nL96: \nL97: cite26†Image†cdn.ca9.uscourts.gov L98: \nL99:   * cite27†For Media L100:   * cite28†Photo and Electronics Policy L101:   * cite29†Privacy Policy L102:   * cite30†Judicial Misconduct†www.ce9.uscourts.gov L103:   * cite31†Your Employee Rights and How to Report Wrongful Conduct†www.ce9.uscourts.gov L104:   * cite32†Vacancies†www.ce9.uscourts.gov L105:   * cite33†Contact L106: \nL107: Looking for U.S. government information and services? cite25†Visit USA.gov --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nForms | United States Bankruptcy Appellate Panel for the Ninth Circuit (https://www.bap9.uscourts.gov/forms/)\nciteturn1414view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: 